00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:05.900
So Compute Engine
is our VM platform.

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:10.570
You can get anywhere from
0.5 to 96 processors,

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:14.540
although we do have larger
processor machines in beta.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:17.540
160, I believe.

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:20.630
And then, anywhere from
0.6 to 624 gigs of RAM.

00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:24.110
And then in beta, we have much
larger machines available.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:27.950
You can attach up to 64
terabytes of standard disk,

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:30.230
or SSD.

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:32.540
And you can do three
terabytes of what

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:36.950
we call attached SSD, which
means in the previous 64

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:39.140
terabyte ones,
those are just disks

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:41.000
that are associated
with the machine.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.030
Those are not, like,
physically attached.

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:47.450
The three terabytes of attached
SSD are kind of on the nose.

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:48.950
They are attached
to the hardware

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:49.610
that you're working with.

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:52.130
Which means you get much higher
performance, and much higher

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:53.790
IOPS out of them.

